From 139026bdbf7864d448a7d8f3258d6418e6115382 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayushman Bhattacharya <ayushman.elixpo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:30:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] avcodec: add RV565 decoder and encoder

RV565 stores video for microcontroller displays as frames already in the
display's pixel format, so a player only decompresses and transfers.
Version 7 of the format declares one of nine pixel formats (rgb565be,
rgb565le, packed rgb444, rgb666, rgb888, gray8, gray4, mono and the
page-ordered mono of SSD1306-class controllers), stores frames as they
are or as zlib streams, and makes each frame a keyframe, the XOR of the
frame with the previous one, or a repeat of it, with a keyframe at least
every 1-255 frames.

A packet is a frame record: a frame type byte and the body. Extradata
carries the pixel format, codec and keyframe interval; without it the
stream is version 6 (rgb565be, zlib, keyframes only). The decoder keeps
the previous frame in the stored layout, since deltas apply to those
bytes, and outputs rgb565be, rgb565le, rgb444be, rgb24, gray or monob,
losslessly for every stored format. It rejects bodies that do not
decode to exactly one frame, and deltas or repeats without a reference.

The encoder stores the input pixel format as it is, or the format chosen
with -format, and writes a repeat for an unchanged frame, otherwise the
smaller of a keyframe and a delta, like the reference encoder; with the
same zlib its output is byte-identical to the reference. -g sets the
keyframe interval (default 1), -compressor stored|zlib the codec and
-compression_level the zlib level (default 1, the level the format's
cost model was measured at).

On the RV565 paper's Big Buck Bunny windows, one keyframe per second
gives 1.10-1.28 MiB for a 90-frame window against 6.12 MiB with only
keyframes (MJPEG q2: 1.84 MiB, lossy), and 4.24-4.65 MiB against 8.54
MiB for a 360-frame window (MJPEG q2: 2.58 MiB), all pixel-exact.

Specification: https://github.com/elixpo/rv565/blob/main/docs/FORMAT.md
Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35935

Signed-off-by: Ayushman Bhattacharya <ayushman.elixpo@gmail.com>
